===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-elīn}}, {{m|gmh|-līn}}, from {{inh|de|goh|-ilī}}, {{m|goh|-ilīn}}.<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=-lein}}</ref> Cognate to {{cog|nl|-lijn}} and {{cog|en|-lin}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/laɪ̯n/|lang=de}}

===Suffix===
{{head|de|suffixes|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|plural|-lein|or|-leins|or|-erlein}}

# {{non-gloss definition|suffix used to create a [[diminutive]] form; e.g., ''Kind'' → ''Kind'''lein'''''}}

====Usage notes====
* In modern Standard German ''-lein'' is less common than, and often replaced by, {{m|de|-chen}}.
* The plural generally remains unchanged as it does with diminutives in ''-chen''. A few nouns with a plural in {{m|de|-er}} may carry the same ending over to the plural diminutive. This is common with {{m|de|Kindlein}} → {{m|de||Kinderlein}} (and equally {{m|de|Kindchen}} → {{m|de||Kinderchen}}); otherwise it is rare. A few nouns referring to people allow a plural in ''-s''. This is common with {{m|de|Fräulein}} → {{m|de||Fräuleins}}; otherwise it is, again, rare.

